From 9472e48f6f74339d1510f65f7308b0fc6cd9ee20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kb <kb@dbi-it.dk>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:06:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] PROTOTYPE: replace the connection and re-run once when
 the server refuses the reset (fix 2b)

Opt-in via SQLCLIENT_REPRO_RESET_RETRY=1. TdsParser marks the outer
SqlConnection when ERROR 4021 arrives on a request that carried the connection
reset bit before the server acknowledged the reset; in that state the server
has executed nothing of the request. SqlCommand.RunExecuteReader (sync) and
the internal-end-and-retry continuation (async) then replace the physical
connection (plain re-open after the class-20 break closed it, with the state
change suppressed as connection resiliency does) and re-run the command once.
Not when a local or ambient transaction is active. ExecuteNonQuery,
BeginTransaction and bulk copy paths are not hooked.

